cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it together with the original PARD-SSM preprint."
title: "PARD in Network Traffic using Switching State Space Models"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-15"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sahilbhekane/PARD-in-Network-Traffic-using-Switching-State-Space-Models-"
url: "https://pard-ssm-probabilistic-attack-regim.vercel.app/"
abstract: >-
  A time-ordered, leakage-free reproduction and re-evaluation of PARD-SSM, a hybrid
  switching state-space model and Random Forest approach to network intrusion
  detection, evaluated on CICIDS2017 and UNSW-NB15. Includes ablation, class-wise
  analysis, exported pipelines, an inference API and a public web application.
keywords:
  - intrusion detection
  - switching state-space models
  - Kalman filter
  - network security
  - CICIDS2017
  - UNSW-NB15
